% A page whose cost is the marks it makes, run through
% run-band-replay-cost-test.sh once into a device holding the whole
% page and once into the band loop.
%
% What the wrapper compares is what the two runs charge the
% interpreter, so this page has to be one whose charge is the marks.
% That is not what a page drawing in a loop is. A loop of rectangle
% fills spends its time in the program and in the fill machinery above
% the device -- a hundred and sixty thousand of them here came to
% within five per cent of each other whichever way the page was put
% out, because the marks are a twentieth of what the page costs and a
% difference in what a mark costs cannot show through that. A page
% built that way says nothing about the replay and would report
% everything is well while the replay got twenty times slower.
%
% Small text is the opposite shape. A glyph is painted pixel by pixel
% against the ground it lands on, so one show of one string is a few
% operators of program and some thousands of marks, and the glyphs are
% cached -- the second line costs its marks and nothing else. That
% makes the marks nearly the whole of the page, which is the only
% arrangement in which the two runs differ by what a mark costs.
%
% The page reports the interpreter time it took, taken after showpage
% because the band loop runs there: the marks are played back when the
% page is put out, so a reading taken before it would be taken before
% the thing being measured had happened. Process startup is outside the
% reading, being the same for both runs and no part of either.

/t0 usertime def

/Helvetica 8 selectfont

% one line of the page, as bytes, so that building it is not part of
% what is being measured
/line 90 string def
0 1 line length 1 sub { line exch 65 put } for

% Enough lines that the reading is tens of times the clock's own
% resolution, and the same lines over again so that no part of the
% total is one-off font work.
1 1 5 {
    pop
    0 8 780 {
        /y exch def
        4 y moveto line show
    } for
} for

showpage

(COST ) print usertime t0 sub 20 string cvs print (\n) print
